// Gas-EOS compressibility verification: the same rate-driven line as
// twoFluidDynamicSlipHoldup with the ideal-gas EOS on (fluid gasR 287,
// rhoG 20 = the reference density the injected rates and the initial state
// refer to). The gas density becomes a per-section transported state: gas
// mass continuity with the Godunov gas volume flux G(a) = vm + (s - vm) a
// - s a^2 and upwind mass fluxes, thermodynamic pressure p = rhoG gasR T
// (T = temperature0 = 300 K, thermal off). Gas accumulates early (holdup
// 0.9 passes only alpha_g vm = 0.1 of gas volume while the inlet injects
// vsg = 0.6), then the state relaxes onto the incompressible steady state:
// gas mass in = out at the injected density pins rhoG* = rhoG = 20 exactly,
// so alpha*/s* match twoFluidDynamicSlipHoldup (root-found here
// independently). The emitted per-cell p is the EOS pressure of the
// transported gas (a rate-driven line's thermodynamic pressure is set by
// the injected mass, not the pressure BCs - the lumped momentum carries no
// local pressure gradient). tests/check_two_fluid.py mode
// compressibleholdup replicates the coupled slip + Godunov holdup + gas
// mass recursion cell by cell (1e-9), checks p = rhoG gasR T0 per section,
// the global gas inventory balance, and the uniform steady state
// (alpha*, s*, rhoG*, imposed phase split, Churchill drop).
//
// Measured anchors (dt 0.05, endTime 80): the replicated inventory lands
// at 89.417 kg/m2 of pipe cross-section; the steady state is uniform
// alpha* = 0.5529126, s* = 0.6185779 with rhoG* = 20.000000 exactly (EOS
// pressure 1.722000e6 Pa) and the Churchill friction drop 4.437184e3 Pa.
fluid
{
    rhoL 1000;
    rhoG 20;
    muL  0.01;
    muG  1e-5;
    gasR 287;
}

pipe
{
    length 10;
    diameter 0.02;
    roughness 0;
    angleDeg 0;
    sections 40;
}

closure
{
    model dynamic;
    interfacialDrag 500;
}

initial
{
    alpha 0.9;
    water 0;
    temperature 300;
}

boundaries
{
    inlet  { type phaseRates; vsl 0.4; vsg 0.6; }
    outlet { type fixedPressure; p 1.0e6; }  // absolute with the EOS on;
                                             // only the backflow ghost uses it
}

time
{
    dt 0.05;
    endTime 80;
    reportEvery 400;
}
